{"type":"step-attempt","step":"design","sessionId":"cecd6e3a-39a7-478e-a5b9-ee213f6939c9","outcome":{"verdict":"success","findingsPath":null,"error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"reason":"Wrote design.md, spec.md, and tasks.md under specrunner/changes/adr-gen-postfix-context/ on branch change/adr-gen-postfix-context-acfa2578.\n\nPlan: adr-gen injects a machine-derived post-fix context block into its initial message. The design reuses the existing prepareRoundContext core hook (sibling of spec-review-prior-round-context), adds a new src/core/step/post-fix-context.ts module (pure fns + derivation via runtimeStrategy.listCommitChangedFiles), a DynamicContext.postFixContext inline field, AdrGenStep wiring (prepareRoundContext + buildMessage + optional postFixContextBlock param), and adr-gen system-prompt priority discipline (ship'd mechanisms belong in Decision/Consequences, never Alternatives Considered).\n\nKey design decisions: D3 scopes rounds to code-fixer only (build/spec-fixer excluded, with rationale); D4 pairs each fixer round with the most-recent findings-bearing run before it; D5 uses all-or-nothing null degradation on any derivation failure (never throws); D6 keeps the block-absent message byte-identical so fixer-less runs and TC-ADR-STEP-01 stay unchanged. reads() review-feedback inconsistency and ADR-body validator are explicitly out of scope. All acceptance criteria (block injection with sabotage check, no-injection path, degradation paths, system-prompt discipline, TC-ADR-STEP-02 update-only, typecheck && test) are mapped to tasks T-01..T-06. No source edits performed — planning only.","status":"success"},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-08-05T13:52:39.610Z","endedAt":"2026-08-05T14:01:28.554Z","commitOid":"e95c91d66d5f0bc55d8eec4819211a3271df4bf3"}
