{"type":"step-attempt","step":"code-review","sessionId":"b574997e-e9fc-447c-86b2-3baf2d1d6fac","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/adr-gen-postfix-context/review-feedback-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":false,"findings":[{"severity":"medium","resolution":"fixable","file":"tests/unit/core/step/adr-gen.test.ts","title":"TC-019 second sub-test is a permanent tautology — sabotage detection for system prompt rule has no teeth","rationale":"The second sub-test of TC-019 uses `expect(typeof ruleIsAbsent).toBe(\"boolean\")` which always passes regardless of whether the system prompt contains the rule. After T-04 implementation, ruleIsAbsent evaluates to false (rule IS present), but the assertion `expect(typeof false).toBe(\"boolean\")` still passes. The comment says to update or remove this test after T-04, but the implementer converted it to a tautology instead. Fix: change to `expect(ADR_GEN_SYSTEM_PROMPT.includes(\"最終実装が正\")).toBe(true)`. Note: TC-009 itself retains real concrete assertions and would fail if T-04 rules were deleted — the issue is limited to TC-019's meta-test function.","line":826}],"evidence":{"checked":23,"skipped":0,"unverified":1},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/step/adr-gen.ts","title":"reads() / message の review-feedback 宣言不整合は pre-existing、スコープ外として設計通りに放置","rationale":"reads() が最新 iteration のみ宣言し、message 本文が review-feedback-*.md (any) を参照する不整合は本 change のスコープ外と design.md に明記されており、意図的に未修正。post-fix ブロックは state findings 由来のため reads() に依存しないことを確認。"}]},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-08-05T14:47:35.011Z","endedAt":"2026-08-05T14:54:23.831Z","commitOid":"2ba182cd47ef53593398f5331497dffea226d4b1"}
